<title>JAPAN: MOF says yen rate within normal mkt fluctuations.</title>
<headline>MOF says yen rate within normal mkt fluctuations.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The current yen exchange rate is moving within normal market fluctuations, Japanese Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Asked about the recent weakening of the yen, Mitsuzuka said: &quot;It's up to the person who sees it to judge whether it is strong or weak. But present rate (moves) are intrinsic moves, moves within the market.&quot;</p>
<p>Mitsuzuka added that exchange rates should reflect economic fundamentals and that one should not overly emphasise temporary market moves.</p>
</text>
